"தம்மைப்","parts":[{"text":"தம்மைப்","lemma":"தம்மைப்","gloss":"themselves"}],"gloss":"themselves","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பிழைத்தோர்ப்","parts":[{"text":"பிழைத்தோர்ப்","lemma":"பிழைத்தோர்ப்","gloss":"those who wronged"}],"gloss":"those who wronged","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பொறுக்குஞ்","parts":[{"text":"பொறுக்குஞ்","lemma":"பொறுக்குஞ்","gloss":"forgiving"}],"gloss":"forgiving","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"செம்மல்","parts":[{"text":"செம்மல்","lemma":"cemmal","gloss":"greatness"}],"gloss":"greatness"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இக்குடிப்","parts":[{"text":"இக்குடிப்","lemma":"இக்குடிப்","gloss":"this lineage"}],"gloss":"this lineage","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"பிறந்தோர்க்","parts":[{"text":"பிறந்தோர்க்","lemma":"பிறந்தோர்க்","gloss":"to those born"}],"gloss":"to those born","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கெண்மை","parts":[{"text":"கெண்மை","lemma":"கெண்மை","gloss":"easy quality"}],"gloss":"easy quality","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காணும்","parts":[{"text":"காணும்","lemma":"kāṇum","gloss":"is seen"}],"gloss":"is seen"},{"surface":"எனக்","parts":[{"text":"எனக்","lemma":"எனக்","gloss":"thus"}],"gloss":"thus","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"காண்டகு","parts":[{"text":"காண்","lemma":"kāṇ","gloss":"to see"},{"text":"தகு","lemma":"taku","gloss":"worthy"}],"gloss":"worthy to see"},{"surface":"மொய்ம்ப","parts":[{"text":"மொய்ம்ப","lemma":"moympa","gloss":"O strong-shouldered one"}],"gloss":"O strong-shouldered one!"},{"surface":"காட்டினை","parts":[{"text":"காட்டினை","lemma":"kāṭṭiṉai","gloss":"you showed"}],"gloss":"you showed"},{"surface":"ஆகலின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகலின்","lemma":"ākaliṉ","gloss":"therefore"}],"gloss":"therefore"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"யானே","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"yāṉ","gloss":"I"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"I indeed"},{"surface":"பிழைத்தனென்","parts":[{"text":"பிழைத்தனென்","lemma":"piḻaittaṉeṉ","gloss":"I erred"}],"gloss":"I erred"},{"surface":"சிறக்கநின்","parts":[{"text":"சிறக்க","lemma":"ciṟakka","gloss":"may it flourish"},{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"may your flourish"},{"surface":"ஆயுள்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயுள்","lemma":"āyuḷ","gloss":"life span"}],"gloss":"life span"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மிக்குவரும்","parts":[{"text":"மிக்கு","lemma":"mikku","gloss":"overflowing"},{"text":"வரும்","lemma":"varum","gloss":"coming"}],"gloss":"overflowing and coming"},{"surface":"இன்னீர்க்","parts":[{"text":"இன்னீர்க்","lemma":"இன்னீர்க்","gloss":"sweet water"}],"gloss":"sweet water","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காவிரி","parts":[{"text":"காவிரி","lemma":"kāviri","gloss":"Kaveri"}],"gloss":"Kaveri"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எக்கர்","parts":[{"text":"எக்கர்","lemma":"ekkar","gloss":"sand dunes"}],"gloss":"sand dunes"},{"surface":"இட்ட","parts":[{"text":"இட்ட","lemma":"iṭṭa","gloss":"deposited"}],"gloss":"deposited"},{"surface":"மணலினும்","parts":[{"text":"மணல்","lemma":"maṇal","gloss":"sand"},{"text":"இனும்","lemma":"iṉum","gloss":"than"}],"gloss":"than the sand"},{"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"pala","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"many indeed"}]}],"literal":"To end the distress of the dwellers upon the earth, / bearing the heat of the burning-rayed sun, / with wind as food, circling with the sun, / so that even the sages with shining matted hair are amazed, escaping the pounce aimed by the curved-winged / sharp-clawed hawk, / entering his refuge, the short-gaited dove's / death fearing, entering the balance scale, / O descendant of the noble one of unlimited generosity! / O younger brother of Killi of generous chariots, who conquered enemies with abundant strength of glory, who holds the long scepter! / O lord of the curved-bow warriors! O noble lord of swift horses / and generous hands! I had a doubt. / All your ancestors who wore garlands of Bauhinia flowers / would never do anything to hurt scholars. But this, / 'Is this proper conduct for you?' thus with anger having spoken, / even though you did not feel hurt by my wronging you, / you felt greatly ashamed as if you yourself had erred. / The greatness of forgiving those who wronged them / is seen as a natural quality for those born in this lineage, thus / O strong-shouldered one, you showed a worthy sight. Therefore, / I indeed erred. May your life span flourish / more than the sand deposited on the dunes / by the overflowing, sweet-watered Kaveri!","translation":"O descendant of the noble king who, to relieve the distress of earth's dwellers, entered the balance scale to save a short-gaited dove fearing death, escaping the pounce of a sharp-clawed, curved-winged hawk—an act that amazed even the sages with shining matted hair who circle with the sun and feed only on wind! O younger brother of Killi of the generous chariots, who conquered foes with great strength and holds the long scepter! O lord of curved-bow warriors, noble lord of swift horses and generous hands! I had a doubt. Your ancestors, who wore garlands of Bauhinia flowers, never did anything to hurt scholars. But when I angrily asked you, 'Is this proper conduct for you?' you did not get angry at my offense. Instead, you felt deeply ashamed as if you yourself had erred. O strong-shouldered one, you showed that forgiving those who wrong them is a natural quality for those born in your noble lineage. Therefore, it is I who erred. May your life flourish for more years than the sands deposited on the dunes by the overflowing, sweet waters of the Kaveri!","modern":"பூமியில் வாழ்பவர்களின் துன்பத்தைத் தீர்க்க, வெயிலைத் தாங்கி, காற்றையே உணவாகக் கொண்டு, சூரியனுடன் வலம் வரும் ஒளிரும் சடையையுடைய முனிவர்களே வியக்கும்படி, வளைந்த சிறகுகளையும் கூர்மையான நகங்களையும் உடைய பருந்தின் தாக்குதலில் இருந்து தப்பித் தன்னிடம் அடைக்கலம் புகுந்த, மெல்ல நடக்கும் புறாவின் மரணத்திற்கு அஞ்சி, தராசுத் தட்டில் ஏறிய அளவற்ற கொடையாளியான சிபியின் வழித்தோன்றலே! பகைவரை வென்ற வலிமையும் புகழும் கொண்ட, தேர்களைக் கொடையாகத் தரும் கிள்ளியின் தம்பியே! நீண்ட செங்கோலை ஏந்தியவனே! வளைந்த வில்லை உடைய வீரர்களின் தலைவனே! விரைந்த குதிரைகளையும் கொடைத் தன்மையையும் உடைய வள்ளலே! எனக்கு ஒரு சந்தேகம் இருந்தது. ஆத்தி மாலை அணிந்த உன்னுடைய முன்னோர்கள் அனைவரும் அறிஞர்கள் வருந்தும்படி எதையும் செய்யமாட்டார்கள். ஆனால், நான் உன்னிடம் கோபத்துடன் 'இது உனக்குத் தகுமா?' என்று வெறுப்புடன் கூறியபோது, நான் செய்த பிழையை நீ பொருட்படுத்தவில்லை. மாறாக, நீயே தவறு செய்தது போலப் பெரிதும் நாணினாய். தமக்குத் தீங்கு செய்தவர்களையும் பொறுத்துக் கொள்ளும் பெருந்தன்மை இந்த வம்சத்தில் பிறந்தவர்களுக்கு இயல்பானது என்பதை, காணத்தக்க உனது தோள் வலிமையால் காட்டினாய். அதனால், நானே தவறு செய்தேன். பெருகி வரும் இனிய நீரைக் கொண்ட காவிரியாறு கரைகளில் சேர்த்த மணலை விடப் பல ஆண்டுகள் உனது ஆயுள் சிறந்து விளங்குவதாக!","explanation":"The poet Tāmappal Kaṇṇaṉār is speaking to Māvaḷattāṉ, the younger brother of the Chola king Nalaṅkiḷḷi, after a game of dice. During the game, the prince hid a die, and the poet angrily threw a die at him. Instead of reacting with royal anger to this insult, the prince showed restraint and felt ashamed of his own initial deception. Realizing his own mistake and the prince's extraordinary patience, the poet sings this song in praise of him. The poet compares the prince's patience to his ancestor King Sibi, who sacrificed his own flesh to save a dove from a hawk, showing that forgiveness is a natural quality of the Chola lineage. The poem concludes with a blessing for a long life, using the image of the abundant sands of the Kaveri river, which symbolizes the fertility and enduring nature of the Chola kingdom.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}